<h3 data-start=3D"2269" data-end=3D"2286">How it works:</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"2287" data-end=3D"2534">
<li data-start=3D"2287" data-end=3D"2352">
<p data-start=3D"2289" data-end=3D"2352"><strong data-start=3D"2289" data-e=
nd=3D"2306">Checkbox hack</strong>: The hidden checkbox stores the toggle s=
tate.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2353" data-end=3D"2427">
<p data-start=3D"2355" data-end=3D"2427"><strong data-start=3D"2355" data-e=
nd=3D"2364">Label</strong> (hamburger) is linked to the checkbox via <code =
data-start=3D"2407" data-end=3D"2426">for=3D"menu-toggle"</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2428" data-end=3D"2510">
<p data-start=3D"2430" data-end=3D"2510">When checked, CSS displays the men=
u (<code data-start=3D"2467" data-end=3D"2508">#menu-toggle:checked + .hamb=
urger + nav</code>).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2511" data-end=3D"2534">
<p data-start=3D"2513" data-end=3D"2534">No JavaScript needed.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"2536" data-end=3D"2668" data-is-last-node=3D"" data-is-onl=
y-node=3D"">If you want, I can make the <strong data-start=3D"2564" data-en=
d=3D"2602">hamburger icon animate into an "X"</strong> when opened =E2=80=
=94 it=E2=80=99ll look much more stylish for your fashion site.</p></div></=
