<p data-start=3D"434" data-end=3D"444"><strong data-start=3D"434" data-end=
=3D"442">Why?</strong></p>
<ul data-start=3D"445" data-end=3D"646">
<li data-start=3D"445" data-end=3D"558">
<p data-start=3D"447" data-end=3D"558"><code data-start=3D"447" data-end=3D=
"454">cover</code> makes sure the image always fills the container (no gaps=
), even if it has to crop parts of the image.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"559" data-end=3D"646">
<p data-start=3D"561" data-end=3D"646"><code data-start=3D"561" data-end=3D=
"570">contain</code> will shrink to fit completely, leaving blank space if =
proportions differ.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"648" data-end=3D"729">If you want the background to slide/=
animate without distortion, it=E2=80=99s better to:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"730" data-end=3D"916">
<li data-start=3D"730" data-end=3D"758">
<p data-start=3D"732" data-end=3D"758">Use <code data-start=3D"736" data-en=
d=3D"743">cover</code> for filling.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"759" data-end=3D"832">
<p data-start=3D"761" data-end=3D"832">Choose hero images with similar aspe=
ct ratios to your hero container.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"833" data-end=3D"916">
<p data-start=3D"835" data-end=3D"916">Or use a <strong data-start=3D"844" =
data-end=3D"870">CSS <code data-start=3D"850" data-end=3D"868">background-i=
mage</code></strong> instead of <code data-start=3D"882" data-end=3D"889">&=
lt;img&gt;</code> for more flexible control.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"918" data-end=3D"1046" data-is-last-node=3D"" data-is-only=
