<h3 data-start=3D"1600" data-end=3D"1617">How it works:</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"1618" data-end=3D"1964">
<li data-start=3D"1618" data-end=3D"1703">
<p data-start=3D"1620" data-end=3D"1703"><strong data-start=3D"1620" data-e=
nd=3D"1645">Images are duplicated</strong> in the HTML so the scroll looks =
seamless when it loops.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1704" data-end=3D"1792">
<p data-start=3D"1706" data-end=3D"1792"><strong data-start=3D"1706" data-e=
nd=3D"1755"><code data-start=3D"1708" data-end=3D"1753">animation: scroll-l=
eft 20s linear infinite;</code></strong> makes it move at a constant speed.=
</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1793" data-end=3D"1880">
<p data-start=3D"1795" data-end=3D"1880">The container has <strong data-sta=
rt=3D"1813" data-end=3D"1836"><code data-start=3D"1815" data-end=3D"1834">o=
verflow: hidden;</code></strong> so images only appear inside the section.<=
/p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1881" data-end=3D"1964">
<p data-start=3D"1883" data-end=3D"1964">The <strong data-start=3D"1887" da=
ta-end=3D"1897"><code data-start=3D"1889" data-end=3D"1895">-50%</code></st=
rong> in <code data-start=3D"1901" data-end=3D"1913">translateX</code> work=
s because we duplicated images exactly once.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1966" data-end=3D"2053">If you want it <strong data-start=
=3D"1981" data-end=3D"2001">faster or slower</strong>, just change <code da=
ta-start=3D"2015" data-end=3D"2020">20s</code> to a smaller or larger numbe=
r.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"2055" data-end=3D"2058">
<p data-start=3D"2060" data-end=3D"2195" data-is-last-node=3D"" data-is-onl=
y-node=3D"">If you want, I can make it <strong data-start=3D"2087" data-end=
=3D"2101">responsive</strong> so it works on all screen sizes without break=
ing the animation. Would you like me to do that?</p></div></div></div></div=
