<h3 data-start=3D"1176" data-end=3D"1193">How it works:</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"1194" data-end=3D"1493">
<li data-start=3D"1194" data-end=3D"1287">
<p data-start=3D"1196" data-end=3D"1287"><strong data-start=3D"1196" data-e=
nd=3D"1240"><code data-start=3D"1198" data-end=3D"1238">display: grid; grid=
-auto-flow: column;</code></strong> =E2=86=92 puts all images in one row wi=
thout wrapping.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1288" data-end=3D"1329">
<p data-start=3D"1290" data-end=3D"1329"><strong data-start=3D"1290" data-e=
nd=3D"1304"><code data-start=3D"1292" data-end=3D"1302">grid-gap</code></st=
rong> =E2=86=92 spacing between logos.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1330" data-end=3D"1390">
<p data-start=3D"1332" data-end=3D"1390"><strong data-start=3D"1332" data-e=
nd=3D"1347"><code data-start=3D"1334" data-end=3D"1345">animation</code></s=
trong> =E2=86=92 moves the entire row from right to left.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1391" data-end=3D"1493">
<p data-start=3D"1393" data-end=3D"1493"><strong data-start=3D"1393" data-e=
nd=3D"1415"><code data-start=3D"1395" data-end=3D"1413">overflow: hidden</c=
ode></strong> on the <code data-start=3D"1423" data-end=3D"1433">.sponsor</=
code> container hides images when they move outside the viewport.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1495" data-end=3D"1630">=E2=9A=A1 <strong data-start=3D"14=
97" data-end=3D"1505">Tip:</strong><br data-start=3D"1505" data-end=3D"1508=
">
If you want the animation to loop seamlessly without a gap, you can <strong=
 data-start=3D"1576" data-end=3D"1603">duplicate the image set</strong> ins=
ide <code data-start=3D"1611" data-end=3D"1629">.sponsor-content</code>.</p=
>
