l <strong data-start=3D"96" data-end=3D"114">using CSS Grid</strong> for la=
yout, the trick is to:</p>
<ol data-start=3D"147" data-end=3D"416">
<li data-start=3D"147" data-end=3D"237">
<p data-start=3D"150" data-end=3D"237">Place the images in a single row usi=
ng <code data-start=3D"189" data-end=3D"204">display: grid</code> with <cod=
e data-start=3D"210" data-end=3D"234">grid-auto-flow: column</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"238" data-end=3D"343">
<p data-start=3D"241" data-end=3D"343">Duplicate the images once so that wh=
en the first set scrolls out, the second set follows seamlessly.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"344" data-end=3D"416">
<p data-start=3D"347" data-end=3D"416">Animate the whole grid container wit=
h <code data-start=3D"385" data-end=3D"413">transform: translateX(...)</cod=
e>.</p>
</li>
</ol>
