t=3D"83" data-end=3D"89">grid</code>, the content will always overflow hori=
zontally unless we duplicate the content and cycle it.</p>
<p data-start=3D"186" data-end=3D"225">To fix this without visible overflow=
:</p>
<ol data-start=3D"227" data-end=3D"474">
<li data-start=3D"227" data-end=3D"292">
<p data-start=3D"230" data-end=3D"292">Use <strong data-start=3D"234" data-=
end=3D"245">flexbox</strong> instead of grid for the animation container.</=
p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"293" data-end=3D"416">
<p data-start=3D"296" data-end=3D"416">Duplicate the logos inside the anima=
tion so that when the first set scrolls out, the second set scrolls in seam=
lessly.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"417" data-end=3D"474">
<p data-start=3D"420" data-end=3D"474">Hide overflow with <code data-start=
=3D"439" data-end=3D"457">overflow: hidden</code> on the parent.</p>
</li>
</ol>
